nI\'m now analyzing Nigeria\'s geopolitical data, particularly focusing on core-periphery dynamics. I\'m noting that the Lagos-Ibadan corridor and the Niger Delta form the resource core, while the arid northeast is the periphery, impacted by desertification and conflict. I\'m also examining the hydrological features and vulnerabilities. I\'m documenting these findings to structure them for presentation.\n\n\n**Structuring Nigeria Data**\n\nI\'m now structuring the population dynamics data, specifically the 1990 pyramid structure for Nigeria. I am focusing on formatting the age cohort data, including male and female percentages, so that it can be integrated into the app. I\'ll ensure that the representation matches the framework for display.\n\n\n**Integrating Nigeria Data**\n\nI\'m now integrating the provided population data for 1990 and 2026 into the existing structure. I\'m focusing on parsing the male and female percentages for each age group, and I\'ll include the administrative region density data and synoptic analysis. I have formatted the data for integration now.\n\n\n**Finalizing Nigeria Data**\n\nI\'m now implementing the 1990 data for Nigeria, including the age cohort percentages and administrative region density. I\'ve integrated this with the current data structure, ensuring correct formatting for display in the app. I\'m focusing now on adding a synoptic analysis.\n\n```text\nI\'ve integrated the provided 1990 population data, now adding the synoptic analysis. I\'m now finishing the formatting and organization within the application. I will focus on the finishing touches now, and move to integration.\n```\n\n\n"
