  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Population Data**\n\nI\'ve successfully retrieved the population data from populationpyramid.net. Initially, I thought it provided percentages, but it\'s raw population counts, interestingly structured as male/female objects with age groups, each with a value (`v`). The next step is to process those values.\n\n\n**Refining Data Processing**\n\nI\'m now focusing on a Node.js script to handle the data transformation. Instead of risky string replacements in `src/data.ts`, I\'m generating a new `src/data.ts` or a new `src/real_data.json` file. It will fetch the JSON, compute the percentages, format them to one decimal place, and simply print the output, regenerating the data structure. It\'s targeted to work for Bangladesh, China, and Nigeria, for 1990 and 2026.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 11
      nanos: 186272501
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
