  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Fixing the Population Pyramid**\n\nI\'ve zeroed in on the `PopulationTab.tsx` file. It seems the population pyramid is inverted and fundamentally incorrect; there\'s a complete absence of male representation. I\'ll need to scrutinize how data is being formatted, especially where male populations are represented as negative values.\n\n\n**Analyzing Chart Orientation**\n\nI\'m now investigating how Recharts renders vertical bar charts with data ordered from youngest to oldest. It seems the default behavior places the youngest cohort at the top, which inverts the population pyramid. I\'m considering reversing the array for correct bottom-to-top rendering, or checking `Recharts` documentation for other options. The absence of male bars appears due to the data\'s structure, so I\'m focusing on the `male` dataKey and its negative values.\n\n\n**Testing Data Handling**\n\nI\'m now focusing on how Recharts handles negative and positive values with `stackId`. While I\'m considering reversing the data order, I\'m leaning more towards testing the stacking behavior first. I suspect that the negative `male` values and positive `female` values, when stacked, might not be rendering as expected. I\'m investigating how the `stackId` interacts with these diverging values, and I\'m also examining the `data.ts` to ensure `male_pct` is correctly populated. I want to confirm `c.male_pct` isn\'t zero.\n\n\n**Verifying Axis Behavior**\n\nI\'ve been re-examining how Recharts handles vertical charts with a category `YAxis`. It appears that reversing the cohort data makes the youngest age group appear at the bottom, which is correct for a population pyramid. I\'m focusing on the Y axis, making sure the zero index in the category axis is at the bottom, as this reverses the axis. I\'m checking the interaction between data order and the default behavior of `Recharts`\'s vertical chart layout to confirm the expected rendering, and confirm my data correctly populates the Y axis.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 9
      nanos: 771126866
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
