    thinking: "**Clarifying the Orientation**\n\nOkay, I\'ve got it. The \"upside down\" issue stems from how Recharts interprets the Y-axis and the `layout=\"vertical\"` setting. It seems the default is to place the younger cohorts at the bottom, which feels counterintuitive in a population pyramid. My understanding is that the Y-axis coordinates might run from bottom to top, rather than top to bottom, making the visual perception \"inverted\".\n\n\n**Addressing the X-axis and Stacking**\n\nI think I\'ve figured out the \"no males\" issue. The X-axis domain `[-10, 10]` might be the culprit, either hiding or misplacing the male bars. Alternatively, the negative and positive stacking with `stackId` could be the issue. Removing `stackId=\"stack\"` could render them side by side instead of overlapping. I\'m going to try reversing the cohorts and removing `stackId`.\n\n\n"
