  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Fetching Population Data Needs**\n\nI\'m currently focused on the population pyramid data retrieval. It appears the timeline slider\'s range (1990-2026) is the key focus, so I am targeting population data for each year within that range. I need to be sure the data structure is efficient.\n\n\n**Expanding Data Timeline Range**\n\nI\'ve decided to broaden the data timeline to 1970-2040 for 16 countries. I\'m focusing on efficiency and realize the data structure is important. Each year for each country has 21 cohorts * 2 values = 42 numbers, and this will total around 3000 numbers per country in total, which seems manageable for the app. I\'m starting to create a script to fetch the data.\n\n\n**Generating Comprehensive Data Set**\n\nI\'m now expanding the data collection. I\'ve compiled a list of target countries and will create a script `fetch_all_years_data.js` to get the `countryId` and then fetch data for each year, 1950-2050 (1970-2040 for the final). The script will process the JSON into a compact format to keep the output manageable, and write to `src/populationData.ts`. I also need to generate mock data for the additional country fields, such as `globalisation_tab` and `economy_tab`.\n\n\n**Creating Country Profiles Now**\n\nI\'m now generating the country profiles, which simplifies the process for new countries. I\'m focusing on creating the script to generate complete profiles, and decided to create the population arrays programmatically. I\'ll need to figure out the slugs at PopulationPyramid.net for a few countries. I\'ve compiled the data to generate, but will keep in mind that I cannot generate every data point.\n\n\n**Refining Data Structures**\n\nI\'m revisiting the data structure to optimize how population data, choropleth maps, and synoptic analyses are handled within each time node. I\'m considering optional fields and interpolation for efficiency, and exploring separating pyramid data into a dictionary for a cleaner structure. My current aim is to simplify and maintain a flexible system for `PopulationTab` data management. I am also investigating the impact on the `DPPlaceProfile` type, so I am looking into how to best make updates there.\n\n\n**Restructuring Data Types**\n\nI\'m now implementing the refactored data structure in `types.ts`, focusing on two key data sets for population analysis. I\'m separating pyramid data into `pyramid_structure` and `timeline_events` for choropleth and synoptic data. I will modify `PopulationTab.tsx` to handle these structures. This will make the application much more maintainable.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 14
      nanos: 990587920
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
