  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Updating the Data Exports**\n\nI\'ve decided to proceed with generating profiles for a list of countries, specifically USA, China, Chad, Niger, Nigeria, UK, Switzerland, Ethiopia, Sudan, Australia, Germany, Mexico, Brazil, DRC, and Bangladesh. Tuvalu is off the list. I\'m modifying `src/data.ts` to export these generated profiles.\n\n\n**Refactoring the Data Fetch**\n\nOkay, I\'ve scrapped the idea of a massive `data.ts` and am now generating individual JSON files per country. My script will fetch the profiles and write them to `public/data/<country>.json`. This allows for dynamic fetching when the user selects a country, resolving the issue of blocking the initial load. It feels cleaner and is far more manageable! I need to refactor `src/App.tsx` to handle the `selectedCountry` state and fetch the relevant JSON on country selection.\n\n\n"
