  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Visualizing Population Pyramids**\n\nI\'m focusing on crafting a visualization for population pyramids, starting with the fundamental structure. The goal is to represent age groups from 0-4 at the bottom to 100+ at the top, along the Y-axis. I\'m placing men on the left, and women on the right, mirroring typical percentage distributions.\n\n\n**Reversing Array for Recharts**\n\nI\'ve realized the data for Recharts needs reversing. Initially, I thought reversing it broke things, but now I understand. The `cohorts` array starts with the youngest age group at the beginning, causing an \"upside-down\" pyramid visualization. To fix this, I need to `.reverse()` the data before passing it to the bar chart. This ensures the youngest age group (0-4) is at the bottom, as expected, with increasing ages as you move up.\n\n\n**Clarifying Pyramid Data Order**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on data ordering. The pyramid appeared upside down, with missing males! The `fetchPyramidYear` script grabs data from the populationpyramid.net API, and then there\'s the initial processing and reversing. The JSON data itself follows the expected age group order (0-4, 5-9, etc.). The reversal causes the youngest age groups to appear at the top in the Recharts vertical bar chart. I\'m now verifying the exact index-to-position mapping in Recharts to confirm if the 0th index is the top or bottom of the chart!\n\n\n**Verifying Recharts Category Axis**\n\nI\'m writing a small test script to confirm Recharts\' default vertical category axis. I need to make sure index 0 corresponds to the bottom. Previously, I reversed the data, which was reported as flipping the pyramid. If the reversal caused the \"upside-down\" visual, I may have fixed the symptom, but not the root cause. The issue of missing males is probably separate, due to a bug with parsing `-c.male_pct` or that some older version of Recharts had issues when `stackOffset=\"sign\"`.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 8
      nanos: 934124640
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
