  planner_response {
    modified_response: "I have rebuilt the spatial data pipeline to properly populate the sub-national density grid across all available case-study countries. \n\nHere is what has been implemented:\n- **Spatial Density Quadrant Matrix**: For each country and every year step (1970\342\200\2232040), the data now securely supplies four distinct data points:\n  1. The integrated **National Average** population density.\n  2. The demographic **Core/Capital** (e.g., *London*, *Lagos*, *Dhaka*).\n  3. A strategic **Semi-Periphery** region.\n  4. A massive, low-density **Periphery** zone.\n- **Dynamic Opacity Scaling**: The frontend logic dynamically recalculates the relative density for the active historic year, shifting the background intensity of each quadrant to visually reflect the polarization and migration between the periphery and the core over time. \n\nThe profiles for all active countries (including China, Nigeria, UK, Australia, Switzerland, etc.) have successfully assimilated this new regional matrix architecture."
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
